          "type": "text",
          "text": "<a href=\"#\"></a>",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "bad8b1fe8a1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Links to nowhere.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "bda38ebddc9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Simplify a lot! This is more re-imagining than it is making a carbon copy. You’ll very much need to simplify and leave things out. You will submit both the original that you used for inspiration and your version, but what we are looking for is for a clever adaptation given the limitations of no javascript.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "b1677323a66",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Note: You can and should use the Chrome DevTools Inspector 🔍 to examine the structure of the original page. You’ll find it is really messy and complicated! Although it is a good idea to inspect individual elements (for instance: a button to see how they styled the borders) it won’t really help you much to try to copy more. If your code blatantly includes un-cited code copied from one of these websites or another students assignment, that will be considered an honor code violation ⚠️. Ask me if you have questions about this.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "b331644ae4b",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "About AI on this lab: you can use an agent — but cite it. If Claude or a tutorial wrote a chunk of your markup, note it in your README.md and be ready to explain what it does and why it's there. Uncited code — from a classmate, a website, or a model — is still an honor code violation ⚠️.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
