          "text": "Three ways to do it — pick one. Option A: render.com — connect your GitHub account and publish this repo as a static site. It has a decent free tier and it works with the private class repo. Option B: GitHub Pages — the same flow you already did in SA0, from this repo's Settings → Pages (check it's offered there; Pages on a private repo depends on the org plan). Option C: Cloudflare Pages — connect this repo from the Cloudflare dashboard and it redeploys on every push. Free, fast, and worth setting up now: we'll be diving into Cloudflare properly later in the term when we get to Workers and Durable Objects, so you'll already have the account. Whichever you pick, this is a separate site from the personal domain you set up in SA0 — don't overwrite that one. All three HOST your site on an internet connected server (ie. “in the cloud”) ☁️.",
